Sticker packs are stored and managed by the core now (core sticker packs
patch); this is the UI for them.

- Composer sticker tab: packs come from getStickerPacks (sorted by name,
  ids instead of paths); deleting removes the pack entry via removeSticker
  instead of deleting the file, which is a blob shared with messages now. A
  bottom bar like the emoji picker's categories shows each pack's first
  sticker (scrolls there, marks the current pack; dropping a sticker on an
  icon moves it there) with Manage Stickers as a gear at its end.
- Empty sticker tab: "Find Sticker Packs" opens the Public Bots directory
  pre-searched for "sticker" (its consent step applies) with a
  community-run note, hidden with the other community suggestions (user
  setting or instance-wide); plus "Import Pack (.zip)" and "Manage".
- Manage Stickers dialog: new/rename/delete/export packs, drag stickers
  between packs (Ctrl/Alt copies; on touch, rest a finger 250ms then drag),
  files dropped in from other apps go into the pack they land on, Move to /
  Copy to in the context menu, add image files, a "Recently Seen" strip of
  chat stickers in no pack yet, packs of the user's other profiles to
  import, and each sticker's emojis as a badge with "Edit Emojis…" (chips
  plus the regular emoji picker).
- A received .zip that holds a sticker pack renders as a pack card. Its
  preview and "Add Sticker Pack" open an inspector with the whole pack
  (emojis from the file names, a big preview on hover/click/Enter) and the
  add button. The check runs in the web runtime (window.__slothfulStickers):
  only downloaded zips up to 15 MiB, once in view, one at a time, cached.
  Other zips keep the plain file tile; the message menu's Open/Export
  Attachment and "Import as Sticker Pack" (also for bigger zips) stay.
  Import failures say why the zip is no pack.
- Backup export says that sticker packs only come back in this app when a
  backup is imported elsewhere, shown only to users who have packs.
- Public Bots dialog takes an initialQuery; the community-suggestions
  setting description names the sticker link too.
